  "root_causes": [
    {
      "id": "layer-map",
      "fixed": true,
      "evidence": "slice.pnr.report.json before: layer_map {path:null, resolution:none}. klt's DEF->GDS merge then numbered routing layers sequentially (M1..: 6/0,8/0,10/0,...,16/0; vias between), which are the deck's Gate 7, Gcut 10, Active 11, N/P select 12/13 layers. After: layer_map resolution exact, M1..M7 on 19..70, vias on 21.. . Count 507,461 -> 125,470.",
      "fix": "layout/pnr/regen.py stages the pinned lambdapdk base/apr/asap7.layermap as klayout/tech/asap7.map and declares assets.klayout in the scratch klt-pdk.json."
    },
    {
      "id": "dbu",
      "fixed": true,
      "fixed_where": "layout/assemble_column.py (#56)",
      "evidence": "The P&R stream is written at dbu 0.001 um; the deck is written for 0.00025. Shipped INVx1 and DFFHQNx1 are clean at 0.00025 and show GATE.S.1/GATE.S.3 only after rescaling to 0.001. Lossless upscaling of the regenerated slice removes GATE.S.3 (102,517) and GATE.S.1 (388) entirely.",
      "disposition": "Addressed at the assembly, not in the slice stream: #56 made layout/assemble_column.py rescale the 0.001 slice into a 0.00025 column, which is the lossless upscale used above. The slice stream itself stays at 0.001 because klt place-and-route has no output-dbu control (gap filed: 2AMLogic/klayout-tools#4482). Running klt drc on layout/slice_routed.gds directly therefore still shows the dbu-driven GATE.S.* counts."
    },
    {
      "id": "router-aux",
      "fixed": false,
      "evidence": "After both effects, 22,711 violations remain on the slice, all on routing: M4.AUX.1/AUX.2 (9,640/9,800, point markers), V4.M5.AUX.2 (1,248), M5/M6.AUX, M4.W.3, M1.S.*, M3.S.2, plus SDT.ACTIVE.AUX.2 (364, inside shipped cells).",
      "disposition": "not resolved here: no generator knob identified that maps to these deck auxiliary rules; recorded for a follow-up."
    }
  ],
